                      %a{:href => "/nlab/edit/representation+theory+-+contents"} Edit this sidebar
          %h1#contents Contents
          .maruku_toc
            %ul
              %li
                %a{:href => "#idea"} Idea
              %li
                %a{:href => "#examples"} Examples
              %ul
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#7DSphericalSpaceFormsWithSpinStructure"}
                    7-dim spherical space forms with
                    = succeed "-structure" do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi Spin
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spin
              %li
                %a{:href => "#properties"} Properties
              %ul
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#HigherGerbesOnSphericalSpaceForms"} Concordances of higher gerbes over spherical space forms
                %ul
                  %li
                    %a{:href => "#Preliminaries"} Preliminaries
                  %li
                    %a{:href => "#TheClassificationTheorem"} The classification theorem
                  %li
                    %a{:href => "#LemmasAndProofs"} Lemmas and proofs
              %li
                %a{:href => "#literature"} Literature
              %ul
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#riemannian_spherical_space_forms"} Riemannian spherical space forms
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#topological_spherical_space_form"} Topological spherical space form
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#smooth_spherical_space_forms"} Smooth spherical space forms
          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A
            %em spherical space form
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotient+space"} quotient space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^n/G
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/round+sphere"} round
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riemannian+manifold"} Riemannian
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-sphere"} n-sphere
            (
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                  %mo ≥
                  %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \geq 2
            ) by a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subgroup"} subgroup
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            of its
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isometry+group"} isometry group
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action"} acts
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+action"} freely
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/properly+discontinuous+action"} properly discontinuously
          %p
            Equivalently, a spherical space form is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riemannian+manifold"} Riemannian manifold
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/constant+function"} constant
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/positive+number"} positive
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sectional+curvature"} sectional curvature
            (an
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elliptic+geometry"} elliptic geometry
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connected+topological+space"} connected
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geodesically+complete+Riemannian+manifold"} geodesically complete
            (see e.g.
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Gadhia07"} Gadhia 07, Lemma 5
          %p
            The spherical space forms are one of three classical examples of
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Clifford-Klein+space+forms"} Clifford-Klein space forms
          %p
            Their classification was raised as an open problem by
            %a{:href => "#Killing1891"} Killing 1891
            and a complete solution was finally compiled by (
            %a{:href => "#Wolf74"}> Wolf 74
            ) (reviewed in
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Gadhia07"} Gadhia 07, section 2.2
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Allock15"} Allock 15
          %p
            Notice that free group actions by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isometries"} isometries
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-spheres"} n-spheres
            are a special case of more general free actions by any
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homeomorphisms"} homeomorphisms
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+actions+on+n-spheres"} group actions on n-spheres
            for more.
          %h2#examples Examples
          %h3#7DSphericalSpaceFormsWithSpinStructure
            7-dim spherical space forms with
            = succeed "-structure" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Spin
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spin
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                  %mo =
                  %mn 7
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n =7
            all the groups
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            in
            %a{:href => "#Wolf74"} Wolf’s classification
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action"} act
            as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subgroups"} subgroups
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/special+orthogonal+group"} SO(8)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mn 8
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^8
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/restriction"} restricted
            to the action on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/7-sphere"} 7-sphere
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 7
                    %mo =
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mn 8
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊂
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mn 8
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^7 = S(\mathbb{R}^8) \subset \mathbb{R}^8
          %p
            Therefore one may consider the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lift"} lift
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi G
                    %mo ^
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \widehat{G}
            of these
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subgroups"} subgroups
            to subgroups of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spin+group"} spin group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Spin
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 8
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi SO
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 8
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spin(8) \to SO(8)
            through the
            = succeed "-projection." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/double+cover"} double cover
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spin+structure"} spin structure
            on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spherical+space+form"} spherical space form
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 7
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^7/G
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi G
                      %mo ^
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \widehat{G}
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Gadhia07"} Gadhia 07
          %p
            Given any such lift
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi G
                      %mo ^
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi Spin
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 8
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \widehat{G} \subset Spin(8)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action"} action
            on the two
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/irreducible+representation"} irreducible
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+spin+representations"} real spin representations
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mn 8
                    %mo ±
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{8}_\pm
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Spin
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 8
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spin(8)
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi N
                    %mo ±
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ≔
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %msub
                    %mi dim
                    %mi ℝ
                  %mrow
                    %mo (
                    %msup
                      %mrow
                        %mo (
                        %msub
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mn 8
                          %mo ±
                        %mo )
                      %mover
                        %mi G
                        %mo ^
                    %mo )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  N_\pm \;\coloneqq\; dim_{\mathbb{R}}\left( \left(\mathbf{8}_{\pm}\right)^{\widehat{G}} \right)
          %p
            for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimension"} dimension
            of the subspace of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spinors"} spinors
            that are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fixed+point"} fixed
            by the action of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi G
                      %mo ^
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \widehat{G}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi G
                    %mo ^
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \widehat{G}
            non-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/trivial+group"}> trivial
            , we have
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi N
                    %mo +
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi N
                    %mo −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi N
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mphantom
                    %mi AA
                  %mtext or
                  %mphantom
                    %mi AA
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi N
                    %mo +
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi N
                    %mo −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 0
                  %mo ,
                  %mi N
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  (N_+, N_-) = (N,0)
                  \\phantom{AA} \text{or} \phantom{AA}
                  (N_+, N_-) = (0,N)
          %p
            and hence up to a choice of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orientation"} orientation
            there is a unique
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi N
                  %mo ∈
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mn 0
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ⋯
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 8
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  N \in \{0,1,\cdots, 8\}
          %p
            associated with each 7-dimensional
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spherical+space+form"} spherical space form
            equipped with
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spin+structure"} spin structure
          %p
            Hence this allows to stratify
            %a{:href => "#Wolf74"} Wolf’s classification
            of 7-dimensional spherical space forms, first into the cases that do and that do not admit any
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spin+structure"} spin structure
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi N
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
            of the space of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Killing+spinors"} Killing spinors
            that they carry.
          %p
            In the case
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi N
                  %mo ≥
                  %mn 4
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N \geq 4
            It turns out that the resulting sub-classification demands
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi G
                    %mo ^
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \widehat{G}
            to be a
            = succeed ";" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+subgroup+of+SU%282%29"} finite subgroup of SU(2)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ADE+classification"} ADE classification
            (
            %a{:href => "#MFFGME09"}> MFFGME 09, Sections 3-7
            ):
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi N
                      %mo =
                      %mn 8
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N = 8
                \: here
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mover
                          %mi G
                          %mo ^
                        %mo =
                        %mi ℤ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mn 2
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \widehat{G} = \mathbb{Z}/2
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cyclic+group+of+order+2"} cyclic group of order 2
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi N
                      %mo =
                      %mn 7
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N = 7
                \: does not occur;
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi N
                      %mo =
                      %mn 6
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N = 6
                \: here
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mover
                        %mi G
                        %mo ^
                      %mo =
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \widehat{G} = \mathbb{Z}/k
                (for
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi k
                        %mo &gt;
                        %mn 2
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k \gt 2)
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cyclic+group"} cyclic group
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi N
                      %mo =
                      %mn 5
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N = 5
                \: here
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mover
                        %mi G
                        %mo ^
                      %mo =
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \widehat{G} =
                a non-
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cyclic+group"} cyclic
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+subgroup+of+SU%282%29"} finite subgroup of SU(2)
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/binary+dihedral+group"} binary dihedral group
                or the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/binary+tetrahedral+group"} binary tetrahedral group
                or
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/binary+octahedral+group"} binary octahedral group
                or
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/binary+icosahedral+group"} binary icosahedral group
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diagonal+action"} acting diagonally
                on
                = succeed ";" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi ℝ
                          %mn 8
                        %mo ≃
                        %mi ℍ
                        %mo ⊕
                        %mi ℍ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^8 \simeq \mathbb{H} \oplus \mathbb{H}
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi N
                      %mo =
                      %mn 4
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N = 4
                \: here
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mover
                        %mi G
                        %mo ^
                      %mo =
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \widehat{G} =
                any
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+subgroup+of+SU%282%29"} finite subgroup of SU(2)
                %em except
                the
