                    \\big)
            %p
          .proof
            %h6 Proof
            %p
              This is the composite of Prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ConcordancesOnSphericalSpaceFormIsMapsOfClassifyingSpaces"}
              with Thm.
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ComparisonMapOfConcordanceInfinityGroupoidsIsEquivalence"}
          .num_remark
            %h6 Remark
            %p
              Cor.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SmoothOkaForMapsOutOfBGIntoBGammaIfGammaIsBraidedTruncated"}
              is of the form of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+Oka+principle"} smooth Oka principle
              but for
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/domain"} domain
              not a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} smooth manifold
              but the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/delooping+groupoid"} delooping groupoid
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+group"} finite group
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %p
              In contrast to the case where the domain is a smooth manifold, equivalences of the form
              %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:TheResultingSmoothOkaLikeEquivalence"} (11)
              fail in general, unless some extra condition like Assumption
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#AssumptionForHigherGerbesOnSphericalSpaceForms"}
              is imposed.
            %p
              For example, in the case that both
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Γ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma
              are
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+Lie+groups"} compact Lie groups
              = succeed "-groupoids" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn ∞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
              %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:TheResultingSmoothOkaLikeEquivalence"} (11)
              are the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hom+infinity-groupoid"}
                hom
                = succeed "-groupoids" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mn ∞
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/global+orbit+category"} global orbit category
              for compact Lie
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariance+groups"} equivariance groups
          %p
          #EquivariantClassifyingSpaceOfPUHBundles.num_remark
            %h6 Example
            %p
              %strong
                (equivariant classifying space of
                = succeed "-bundles)" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi PU
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi ℋ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} PU(\mathcal{H})
              %br/
              In the case that
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/structure+group"} structure group
                  is
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Γ
                        %mo =
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma =
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/PU%28%E2%84%8B%29"} PU(ℋ)
              %li
                %p
                  the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariance+group"} equivariance group
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi G
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
                  is a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+group"} finite group
                  which has any
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+action"} free action
                  on any
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-sphere"} n-sphere
                  for
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo ≥
                        %mn 4
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \geq 4
            %p
              Cor.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SmoothOkaForMapsOutOfBGIntoBGammaIfGammaIsBraidedTruncated"}
              immediately implies that the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+groups"} homotopy groups
            .maruku-equation
