            %p
              It follows by
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-out-of-3"} 2-out-of-3
              that also the function on the right is a bijection:
            #eq:CocyclesToClassifyingMapsIsBijection.maruku-equation
              %span.maruku-eq-number (12)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi τ
                      %mn 0
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} TopFunc
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.8em", :minsize => "1.8em"} (
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo +
                        %mn 2
                    %mo ×
                    %mi G
                    %mo ⇉
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo +
                        %mn 2
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                    %mi Γ
                    %mo ⇉
                    %mo *
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.8em", :minsize => "1.8em"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo ∼
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi τ
                      %mn 0
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Maps
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.8em", :minsize => "1.8em"} (
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Shp
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo +
                        %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mspace{:width => "negativethinmathspace"}
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi B
                    %mi Γ
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.8em", :minsize => "1.8em"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\tau_0
                    \\,
                    \\mathrm{TopFunc}
                    \\Big(
                    \\big(
                    S^{n+2} \times G \rightrightarrows S^{n+2}
                    \\big)
                    ,\,
                    \\big(
                    \\Gamma \rightrightarrows \ast
                    \\big)
                    \\Big)
                    \\xrightarrow{\;\; \sim \;\;}
                    \\tau_0
                    \\,
                    \\mathrm{Maps}
                    \\Big(
                    \\mathrm{Shp}
                    \\big(
                    S^{n+2} /\!/ G
                    \\big)
                    ,\,
                    B \Gamma
                    \\Big)
            %p
              Observe that the composite of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+homotopy+equivalence"} equivalences
              in
              %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:MapsIntoTruncatedBGammaSeeSphericalSpaceFormAsClassifyinSpace"} (9)
              is again the morphism induced by pre-composition with
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo +
                        %mn 2
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mi p
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo *
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mtext or
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo *
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mi i
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo +
                        %mn 2
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    S^{n+2} \xrightarrow{\; p \;} \ast
                    \\;\;\;\;
                    \\text{or}
                    \\;\;\;\;
                    \\ast \xrightarrow{\; i \;} S^{n+2}
                    \\,.
            %p
              Therefore, by
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functoriality
              of the
              = succeed "-operation" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nerve"} nerve
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+realization+of+simplicial+topological+spaces"} topological realization
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commuting+diagram"} diagram commutes
