            %p Here
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  the top and bottom horizontal functions are bijections by
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:CocyclesToClassifyingMapsIsBijection"} (12)
              %li
                %p
                  the right vertical functions are bijections by
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:MapsIntoTruncatedBGammaSeeSphericalSpaceFormAsClassifyinSpace"} (9)
            %p
              By commutativity of the total rectangle, this implies that the left vertical functions exhibit a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/retraction"} retraction
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/surjective"} surjective
            %p
              But the bottom left function is clearly also
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/injective"} injective
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo +
                        %mn 2
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi Γ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi \colon S^{n+2} \xrightarrow{\;} \Gamma
              is a Cech coboundary between Cech cocycles that are constant along
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi S
                        %mrow
                          %mi n
                          %mo +
                          %mn 2
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^{n+2}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi(\ast)
              conjugates the corresponding
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+homomorphisms"} group homomorphisms
              into each other.
            %p Therefore the bottom left morphism is both injective as well as surjective, hence bijective.
          %p
            More generally, the analogous conclusion evidently still holds for
            = succeed "-principal" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Γ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+product+space"} topological product space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
