                    \\\
                    S^{n+2}/G \times \Delta^1
                    \&amp;=&amp;
                    S^{n+2}/G \times \Delta^1
                    }
            %p
          .proof
            %h6 Proof
            %p
              By the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classifying+space"} classification theory
              of principal bundles (or, more concretely, by the proof of
              = succeed ")," do
                %a{:href => "concordance#ConcordantTopologicalPrincipalBundlesAreIsomorphic"} this Prop.
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cylinder"} cylinder
              like
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo +
                        %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi G
                    %mo ×
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^{n+2}/G  \times [0,1]
              is isomorphic to the constant re-extension of its restriction to one end of the cylinder. With the given 1-morphism denoted as in Exp.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#OneMorphismInShapeOfMappingStackFromSphericalSpaceFormToBGamma"}
              we write
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℓ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \ell
              for such an isomorphism onto its
              = succeed "-component:" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi P
                        %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P_0
