          %h3#riemannian_spherical_space_forms Riemannian spherical space forms
          %p
            Historically and by default, spherical space forms are understood in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riemannian+geometry"} Riemannian geometry
            hence with finite groups acting (freely and) by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isometries"} isometries
            on
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-spheres"} n-spheres
          %p Historical articles:
          %ul
            %li#Killing1891
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Wilhelm+Killing"}> Wilhelm Killing
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Ueber die Clifford-Klein’schen Raumformen
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/BF01206655"} doi:10.1007/BF01206655
          %p Solution of the classification problem:
          %ul
